WEBVTT

NOTE English descriptive captions for the silent FlashLearn PWD Gaze Control demo (recorded on a tablet, nobody touching the screen).

00:00.000 --> 00:05.100
Gaze Control is on. Nobody touches the screen: the learner turns their head to move the highlight.

00:05.100 --> 00:12.400
Right to the Settings gear, then down, row by row.

00:12.400 --> 00:18.300
A long, deliberate blink opens what is lit — here, the word decks.

00:18.300 --> 00:23.900
The same head moves work on every screen.

00:23.900 --> 00:34.200
Another learner can’t move their head. With scanning, each row lights up in turn, and the camera stays off.

00:34.200 --> 00:38.300
One press of a switch goes into the lit row; a second opens the Talk Board.

00:38.300 --> 00:44.100
On the Talk Board, Add puts the lit picture into the sentence…

00:44.100 --> 00:51.700
…Next moves to the next picture, and Add again: “Hello · Good morning”.

00:51.700 --> 00:53.900
Speak reads the sentence aloud — all with one button.
